<p>Greetings SCP community,<br />
it is a pleasure to finally take that step and join the wiki.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Here's&nbsp;my&nbsp;story&nbsp;of&nbsp;how&nbsp;I&nbsp;decided&nbsp;to&nbsp;join&nbsp;this&nbsp;wiki</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Here's&nbsp;my&nbsp;story&nbsp;of&nbsp;how&nbsp;I&nbsp;decided&nbsp;to&nbsp;join&nbsp;this&nbsp;wiki</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I have been reading on and off on the SCP wiki for years now, the origins of which I've long forgotten (must've been Containment Breach videos on Youtube). I decided to join after I started watching <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tanhony" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(776854); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=776854&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1594350517" alt="Tanhony" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=776854)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tanhony" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(776854); return false;">Tanhony</a></span>'s <a href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLbNC2DQDk3O0QaODHpUOATH_GzsNe1aka" target="_blank">Discovering SCP</a> series and they discussed voting and fixing articles. I decided <em>&quot;I should at least join to vote for the articles I've enjoyed reading,&quot;</em> so I finally joined after years of consideration.</p>
<p>I was torn between the Writers/Readers/Explorers intro forums but decided on &quot;Reader&quot; since that's what I see myself mostly doing. While I want to write SCPs, tales, original characters, etc. I'm not productive so my ideas will stay as headcanon until I finally write something. On the other hand, explorer doesn't really make sense to me since it seems like <em>less reader, more &quot;other.&quot;</em></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;About&nbsp;myself</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;About&nbsp;myself</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ul>
<li>I'm male</li>
<li>I'm a college student</li>
<li>I have some Computer Science know-how (or I can at least learn and use it very quickly)</li>
<li>I have mild <a href="https://www.psychologytoday.com/us/basics/aspergers-syndrome" target="_blank">Asperger's Syndrome</a>.</li>
<li>I have no experience writing on forums or participating in an online community.</li>
<li>I believe in being formal and professional at all times so I have high standards in both writings and myself (hence all the editing and links in this post and the fact I spent over an hour writing and editing it).</li>
<li>My favorite aspects about the SCP Universe seem to mostly float towards space (<em>a great expanse to explore</em>) and history (<em>the sequence of events that lead to other events</em>). But in the end, I love the incredibly original creativity of the community and the uni-/multi-verse they've crafted.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Question&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;month</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Question&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;month</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>To answer <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1404533&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1594350517" alt="Zyn" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1404533)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;">Zyn</a></span>'s question:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>what is your favorite homemade food?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The answer (the only answer that comes to mind at the moment) is <strong>pizza bagels</strong>.<br />
Pizza bagels are simply toasted bagel halves with tomato paste (not pizza sauce), garlic powder, Italian seasoning, and then mozzarella cheese broiled on top. I usually make them for myself except when I feel like It would be a good family meal to make. A common complaint is that I put too much tomato paste on the bagels but I would rather use up the entire can of tomato paste then have the leftover paste go bad (I'm not fond of having leftovers in the fridge).</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
(I hope I get notified if this post gets replied to because I might not check otherwise)
<p>EDIT: Looks like you don't get notified when someone replies to your forum post. Checking the forums in the future seems to be the only way to check for new posts/replies. If there's a way to get notified I have no idea what it is.</p>

